    "body": "## Problem\n\nIf the cursors are cleared in Insert-mode (e.g. `nvim_buf_clear_namespace()` on `nvim.multicursor` from a mapping), the text already previewed at them disappears on `<Esc>`. Ending the session deletes the preview at every region, then replays the typed keys only at the cursors that still exist, so the removed ones end up with nothing.\n\n## Solution\n\nRemember which cursor each preview region belongs to. Once a cursor is gone, its preview stays as plain text and is no longer updated, deleted or replayed. This also covers a partial clear: the removed cursors keep what they had, the rest still replay as before.\n\nFixes #42502\n",
